update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["The process of a caterpillar transforming into a moth is one of the most amazing phenomena in nature. This process is called complete metamorphosis.", "The caterpillar first becomes a pupa and completely changes its body inside a hard shell. At this time, the caterpillar''s body melts and is remade into a new form. This process usually takes about 2-3 weeks.", "Truly remarkable things happen inside the pupa. The caterpillar''s muscles and organs are all broken down, and the moth''s wings and legs grow anew. Through these changes, it becomes a completely different organism.", "In Korea, you can easily observe this transformation process in spring and summer. Especially when you discover a moth''s pupa in a park or mountain, you can feel the mysterious power of nature."], "sentences": [{"text": "애벌레가 나방으로 변하는 과정은 자연의 가장 놀라운 현상 중 하나예요.", "translation": "The process of caterpillars transforming into moths is one of nature''s most amazing phenomena.", "vocab": [{"ko": "애벌레", "en": "caterpillar"}, {"ko": "나방", "en": "moth"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be amazing; to be astonishing"}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 과정", "exp": "Relative clause modifier. ''변하다'' (change) + relative participle ~는 forms a noun modifier describing the process.", "example_in_sentence": "변하는 과정"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~중 하나", "exp": "Among/one of. Indicates something is one item within a category or group.", "example_in_sentence": "현상 중 하나예요"}]}, {"text": "이 과정을 완전변태(完全變態)라고 부릅니다.", "translation": "This process is called complete metamorphosis.", "vocab": [{"ko": "완전변태", "en": "complete metamorphosis"}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call, to name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~라고 부르다", "exp": "Quotative ~라고 + verb 부르다. Used to indicate how something is called or named.", "example_in_sentence": "완전변태(完全變態)라고 부릅니다"}]}, {"text": "애벌레는 먼저 번데기가 되어 단단한 껍질 속에서 몸을 완전히 바꿔요.", "translation": "First, the caterpillar becomes a pupa and completely changes its body inside a hard shell.", "vocab": [{"ko": "번데기", "en": "pupa"}, {"ko": "단단하다", "en": "to be hard; to be firm"}, {"ko": "껍질", "en": "shell, skin"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 (and then)", "exp": "Links two actions in sequence. 되다 → 되어 = becomes (a pupa) and then ...", "example_in_sentence": "번데기가 되어"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~속에서", "exp": "Inside, within. Indicates location or environment where an action takes place.", "example_in_sentence": "껍질 속에서"}]}, {"text": "이때 애벌레의 몸은 녹아서 새로운 형태로 다시 만들어집니다.", "translation": "At this time, the caterpillar''s body dissolves and is remade into a new form.", "vocab": [{"ko": "녹다", "en": "to melt, to dissolve"}, {"ko": "형태", "en": "form, shape"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~어/아서 (sequential connective)", "exp": "Connects sequential actions with reason or cause. 녹다 → 녹아서 (melts, and); introduces the result of melting.", "example_in_sentence": "녹아서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어/아지다 (passive/state change)", "exp": "Passive voice or state change. 만들다 → 만들어지다 (is made, becomes made); indicates the body undergoes transformation.", "example_in_sentence": "만들어집니다"}]}, {"text": "이 과정은 보통 2-3주 정도 걸려요.", "translation": "This process usually takes about 2-3 weeks.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정도", "en": "approximately, about"}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to take (time)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~정도 걸리다", "exp": "Takes approximately (a duration). Collocates to express time requirements.", "example_in_sentence": "2-3주 정도 걸려요"}]}, {"text": "번데기 안에서는 정말 놀라운 일이 일어나요.", "translation": "Inside the pupa, truly amazing things happen.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be amazing; to be astonishing"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, to occur"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~안에서", "exp": "Inside, within. Marks the location or environment where an event occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "번데기 안에서"}]}, {"text": "애벌레의 근육과 장기가 모두 분해되고, 나방의 날개와 다리가 새롭게 자라납니다.", "translation": "The caterpillar''s muscles and organs are all broken down, and the moth''s wings and legs grow anew.", "vocab": [{"ko": "근육", "en": "muscle"}, {"ko": "장기", "en": "organ"}, {"ko": "분해되다", "en": "to decompose, to break down"}, {"ko": "자라나다", "en": "to grow (out)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (coordinate connector)", "exp": "Connects two parallel clauses. 분해되다 → 분해되고; links decomposition and growth as simultaneous processes.", "example_in_sentence": "분해되고"}]}, {"text": "이런 변화를 통해 완전히 다른 생물체가 되는 거예요.", "translation": "Through such changes, it becomes a completely different organism.", "vocab": [{"ko": "변화", "en": "change, transformation"}, {"ko": "생물체", "en": "organism"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 통해", "exp": "Through, via. Indicates the means or medium by which something is achieved.", "example_in_sentence": "변화를 통해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 거예요 (explaining)", "exp": "Explains or sums up what is happening. 되다 → 되는 거예요 = (that is how) it becomes ...", "example_in_sentence": "되는 거예요"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 봄과 여름에 이런 변화 과정을 쉽게 관찰할 수 있어요.", "translation": "In Korea too, one can easily observe such transformation processes in spring and summer.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관찰하다", "en": "to observe"}, {"ko": "쉽게", "en": "easily"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 관찰하다 → 관찰할 수 있어요 = can observe.", "example_in_sentence": "관찰할 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "특히 공원이나 산에서 나방의 번데기를 발견하면 자연의 신비로운 힘을 느낄 수 있습니다.", "translation": "In particular, if you find a moth pupa in a park or on a mountain, you can feel the mysterious power of nature.", "vocab": [{"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover, to find"}, {"ko": "신비롭다", "en": "to be mysterious"}, {"ko": "힘", "en": "power, force"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if, when)", "exp": "Sets up a condition. 발견하다 → 발견하면 = if you find.", "example_in_sentence": "발견하면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 느끼다 → 느낄 수 있습니다 = can feel.", "example_in_sentence": "느낄 수 있습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "애벌레", "en": "caterpillar", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나방", "en": "moth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be amazing; to be astonishing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완전변태", "en": "complete metamorphosis", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call, to name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "번데기", "en": "pupa", "note": ""}, {"ko": "단단하다", "en": "to be hard; to be firm", "note": ""}, {"ko": "껍질", "en": "shell, skin", "note": ""}, {"ko": "녹다", "en": "to melt, to dissolve", "note": ""}, {"ko": "형태", "en": "form, shape", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정도", "en": "approximately, about", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to take (time)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen, to occur", "note": ""}, {"ko": "근육", "en": "muscle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "장기", "en": "organ", "note": ""}, {"ko": "분해되다", "en": "to decompose, to break down", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자라나다", "en": "to grow (out)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change, transformation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생물체", "en": "organism", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관찰하다", "en": "to observe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쉽게", "en": "easily", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover, to find", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신비롭다", "en": "to be mysterious", "note": ""}, {"ko": "힘", "en": "power, force", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~는 과정", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Relative clause modifier. ''변하다'' (change) + relative participle ~는 forms a noun modifier describing the process.", "ex_ko": "애벌레가 나방으로 변하는 과정은 자연의 가장 놀라운 현상 중 하나예요.", "ex_en": "The process of caterpillars transforming into moths is one of nature''s most amazing phenomena."}, {"name": "~라고 부르다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotative ~라고 + verb 부르다. Used to indicate how something is called or named.", "ex_ko": "이 과정을 완전변태(完全變態)라고 부릅니다.", "ex_en": "This process is called complete metamorphosis."}, {"name": "~아/어 (and then)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Links two actions in sequence. 되다 → 되어 = becomes (a pupa) and then ...", "ex_ko": "애벌레는 먼저 번데기가 되어 단단한 껍질 속에서 몸을 완전히 바꿔요.", "ex_en": "First, the caterpillar becomes a pupa and completely changes its body inside a hard shell."}, {"name": "~어/아서 (sequential connective)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connects sequential actions with reason or cause. 녹다 → 녹아서 (melts, and); introduces the result of melting.", "ex_ko": "이때 애벌레의 몸은 녹아서 새로운 형태로 다시 만들어집니다.", "ex_en": "At this time, the caterpillar''s body dissolves and is remade into a new form."}, {"name": "~어/아지다 (passive/state change)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Passive voice or state change. 만들다 → 만들어지다 (is made, becomes made); indicates the body undergoes transformation.", "ex_ko": "이때 애벌레의 몸은 녹아서 새로운 형태로 다시 만들어집니다.", "ex_en": "At this time, the caterpillar''s body dissolves and is remade into a new form."}, {"name": "~고 (coordinate connector)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connects two parallel clauses. 분해되다 → 분해되고; links decomposition and growth as simultaneous processes.", "ex_ko": "애벌레의 근육과 장기가 모두 분해되고, 나방의 날개와 다리가 새롭게 자라납니다.", "ex_en": "The caterpillar''s muscles and organs are all broken down, and the moth''s wings and legs grow anew."}, {"name": "~는 거예요 (explaining)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Explains or sums up what is happening. 되다 → 되는 거예요 = (that is how) it becomes ...", "ex_ko": "이런 변화를 통해 완전히 다른 생물체가 되는 거예요.", "ex_en": "Through such changes, it becomes a completely different organism."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 관찰하다 → 관찰할 수 있어요 = can observe.", "ex_ko": "한국에서도 봄과 여름에 이런 변화 과정을 쉽게 관찰할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "In Korea too, one can easily observe such transformation processes in spring and summer."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if, when)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Sets up a condition. 발견