"ex_en": "Ants are small, but they lift things heavier than their own bodies."}, {"name": "~보다 (comparison particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks the comparative standard. Indicates ''compared to'' or ''more than''. Follows the noun 사람.", "ex_ko": "개미는 작지만 자기 몸보다 무거운 것을 들어요.", "ex_en": "Ants are small, but they lift things heavier than their own bodies."}, {"name": "~도 (inclusive particle; ''even'')", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Adds emphasis meaning ''also'' or ''too''. Marks 우리 as included in the group that can learn.", "ex_ko": "곰은 큰 바위도 밀 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Bears can even push large rocks."}, {"name": "~의 (possessive particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks possession or attribution. Connects 동물들 with 힘, indicating ''the power of animals''.", "ex_ko": "동물들의 힘은 정말 대단해요.", "ex_en": "The power of animals is truly amazing."}, {"name": "~나 (emphasizing particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Emphasizes the quantity or degree. After a number/amount, it strengthens the comparison meaning ''as much as'' or ''up to''.", "ex_ko": "고릴라는 사람보다 10배나 힘이 세요.", "ex_en": "Gorillas are 10 times stronger than humans."}, {"name": "~기 위해 (in order to)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Shows purpose. 살다 → 살기 위해 = in order to live.", "ex_ko": "동물들은 살기 위해 이런 힘을 써요.", "ex_en": "Animals use this power in order to live."}, {"name": "~거나 (alternative connective)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Connects two alternative actions. Converts verb 찾다 into 찾거나, indicating ''or'' between two options.", "ex_ko": "먹이를 찾거나 집을 만들 때 필요해요.", "ex_en": "It is needed when finding food or building a home."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 때 (when)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks the time when something happens. 만들다 → 만들 때 = when making.", "ex_ko": "먹이를 찾거나 집을 만들 때 필요해요.", "ex_en": "It is needed when finding food or building a home."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mom3sj72df6t' and md5(translation) = '17667ebfa38bfec9eb6e36ddb871f4bb';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 1963, there was an interesting experiment in the United States. Passengers on an airplane were told that the pilot was a woman. At that time, researchers observed the passengers'' reactions. In the 1960s, female pilots were very rare. Most people believed that pilots should be men. So this experiment was very special. Passengers were surprised when they heard the news about the female pilot. Some people showed signs of worry. However, the airplane operated safely. This experiment revealed gender bias. Now, the number of female pilots has increased significantly. Female pilots are also active in Korea.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "1963년에 미국에서 흥미로운 실험이 있었어요.", "translation": "In 1963, there was an interesting experiment in the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting"}, {"ko": "실험", "en": "experiment"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist; to be"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending indicating a completed action or state in informal polite speech. 있다 → 있었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject particle)", "exp": "Marks the subject. After a consonant use 이: 실험 → 실험이.", "example_in_sentence": "실험이"}]}, {"text": "비행기 승객들에게 조종사가 여성이라고 말했어요.", "translation": "They told the airplane passengers that the pilot was a woman.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비행기", "en": "airplane"}, {"ko": "승객", "en": "passenger"}, {"ko": "조종사", "en": "pilot"}, {"ko": "여성", "en": "woman; female"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "Dative particle indicating the recipient or target of an action.", "example_in_sentence": "승객들에게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이라고", "exp": "Quotative particle used to report or quote a statement or assertion. 여성이다 → 여성이라고.", "example_in_sentence": "여성이라고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending. 말하다 → 말했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "말했어요"}]}, {"text": "그때 승객들의 반응을 관찰했어요.", "translation": "At that time, they observed the passengers'' reactions.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그때", "en": "at that time; then"}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction; response"}, {"ko": "관찰하다", "en": "to observe"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle indicating ownership or association.", "example_in_sentence": "승객들의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Accusative particle marking the direct object.", "example_in_sentence": "반응을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending. 관찰하다 → 관찰했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "관찰했어요"}]}, {"text": "1960년대에는 여성 조종사가 매우 드물었어요.", "translation": "In the 1960s, female pilots were very rare.", "vocab": [{"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare; uncommon"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very; extremely"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "Temporal particle with contrastive nuance indicating a specific time period.", "example_in_sentence": "1960년대에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending for adjectives. 드물다 → 드물었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "드물었어요"}]}, {"text": "대부분의 사람들은 조종사는 남성이어야 한다고 생각했어요.", "translation": "Most people thought that pilots should be male.", "vocab": [{"ko": "대부분", "en": "most; the majority"}, {"ko": "남성", "en": "man; male"}, {"ko": "생각하다", "en": "to think"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive particle indicating belonging or association.", "example_in_sentence": "대부분의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다 (must)", "exp": "Expresses necessity. With 이다: 남성이다 → 남성이어야 한다 = must be a man.", "example_in_sentence": "남성이어야 한다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 생각하다 (to think that ~)", "exp": "Reports what someone thinks. 한다 → 한다고 생각했어요 = thought that (pilots) had to (be men).", "example_in_sentence": "한다고 생각했어요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 이 실험이 매우 특별했어요.", "translation": "Therefore, this experiment was very special.", "vocab": [{"ko": "그래서", "en": "so; therefore; that is why"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending for adjectives. 특별하다 → 특별했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "특별했어요"}]}, {"text": "승객들은 여성 조종사 소식을 듣고 놀랐어요.", "translation": "The passengers were surprised when they heard the news about the female pilot.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소식", "en": "news; information"}, {"ko": "듣다", "en": "to hear; to listen"}, {"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised; to be astonished"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending linking two sequential actions. 듣다 → 듣고.", "example_in_sentence": "듣고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "Marks a completed past action. 놀라다 → 놀랐어요 = were surprised.", "example_in_sentence": "놀랐어요"}]}, {"text": "어떤 사람들은 걱정하는 모습을 보였어요.", "translation": "Some people looked worried.", "vocab": [{"ko": "어떤", "en": "some; certain; which"}, {"ko": "걱정하다", "en": "to worry"}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance; look; state"}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to show"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Present tense participle modifying the noun. 걱정하다 → 걱정하는.", "example_in_sentence": "걱정하는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Accusative particle marking the direct object.", "example_in_sentence": "모습을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending. 보이다 → 보였어요.", "example_in_sentence": "보였어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 비행기는 안전하게 운항했어요.", "translation": "However, the plane flew safely.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but; however"}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe"}, {"ko": "운항하다", "en": "to operate (an aircraft); to fly"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 (adverb form)", "exp": "Turns a describing word into an adverb. 안전하다 → 안전하게 = safely.", "example_in_sentence": "안전하게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending. 운항하다 → 운항했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "운항했어요"}]}, {"text": "이 실험은 성별에 대한 편견을 보여줬어요.", "translation": "This experiment showed prejudice about gender.", "vocab": [{"ko": "성별", "en": "gender; sex"}, {"ko": "편견", "en": "prejudice; bias"}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to demonstrate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 대한 (about, toward)", "exp": "Links a topic to the noun that follows. 성별에 대한 편견 = prejudice about gender.", "example_in_sentence": "성별에 대한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Accusative particle marking the direct object.", "example_in_sentence": "편견을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending. 보여주다 → 보여줬어요.", "example_in_sentence": "보여줬어요"}]}, {"text": "지금은 여성 조종사가 많이 늘어났어요.", "translation": "Now, the number of female pilots has increased greatly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금", "en": "now; at present"}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "much; many; greatly"}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "to increase; to grow"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic, contrast)", "exp": "Marks the topic; here it contrasts now with the past. 지금은 = now (unlike before).", "example_in_sentence": "지금은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending indicating a completed change of state. 늘어나다 → 늘어났어요.", "example_in_sentence": "늘어났어요"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 여성 조종사들이 활동하고 있어요.", "translation": "Female pilots are also active in Korea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "한국", "en": "Korea"}, {"ko": "활동하다", "en": "to be active; to engage in activity"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서도", "exp": "Locative particle with addition marker indicating a place and addition of scope.", "example_in_sentence": "한국에서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect construction indicating an ongoing or continuous state or action. 활동하다 → 활동하고 있다.", "example_in_sentence": "활동하고 있어요"}]}], "version": 