종사는 남성이어야 한다고 생각했어요.", "ex_en": "Most people thought that pilots should be male."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connective ending linking two sequential actions. 듣다 → 듣고.", "ex_ko": "승객들은 여성 조종사 소식을 듣고 놀랐어요.", "ex_en": "The passengers were surprised when they heard the news about the female pilot."}, {"name": "~는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present tense participle modifying the noun. 걱정하다 → 걱정하는.", "ex_ko": "어떤 사람들은 걱정하는 모습을 보였어요.", "ex_en": "Some people looked worried."}, {"name": "~게 (adverb form)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Turns a describing word into an adverb. 안전하다 → 안전하게 = safely.", "ex_ko": "하지만 비행기는 안전하게 운항했어요.", "ex_en": "However, the plane flew safely."}, {"name": "~에 대한 (about, toward)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Links a topic to the noun that follows. 성별에 대한 편견 = prejudice about gender.", "ex_ko": "이 실험은 성별에 대한 편견을 보여줬어요.", "ex_en": "This experiment showed prejudice about gender."}, {"name": "~은/는 (topic, contrast)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the topic; here it contrasts now with the past. 지금은 = now (unlike before).", "ex_ko": "지금은 여성 조종사가 많이 늘어났어요.", "ex_en": "Now, the number of female pilots has increased greatly."}, {"name": "~에서도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locative particle with addition marker indicating a place and addition of scope.", "ex_ko": "한국에서도 여성 조종사들이 활동하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Female pilots are also active in Korea."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mom3t28cybq3' and md5(translation) = '00458c0a1e957b9528c61d11706648aa';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A man living in California, USA uses a special method. He flies a drone to guide delivery drivers who cannot find his house.", "This man''s house is difficult to find. That''s why delivered food and packages often arrive late. It''s because delivery drivers get lost on the way.", "He attached lights to the drone. When a delivery driver arrives, he sends the drone up into the sky. The drone guides the way to his house.", "This method is very effective. Now delivery drivers can easily find his house. He is able to receive deliveries faster."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국 캘리포니아에 사는 한 남성이 특별한 방법을 사용해요.", "translation": "A man living in California, USA uses a special method.", "vocab": [{"ko": "캘리포니아", "en": "California"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 살다 → 사는 남성 = a man who lives (there); ㄹ drops before 는.", "example_in_sentence": "사는 한 남성"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요 (polite present ending)", "exp": "Indicates statement in polite/conversational tone. Verb 사용하다 → 사용해요.", "example_in_sentence": "사용해요"}]}, {"text": "집을 찾지 못하는 배달 기사들을 위해 드론(drone)을 날려요.", "translation": "He flies a drone for delivery workers who can''t find his house.", "vocab": [{"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find"}, {"ko": "배달", "en": "delivery"}, {"ko": "드론", "en": "drone"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 못하다 (negation with inability)", "exp": "Indicates inability or failure to perform an action. Verb 찾다 → 찾지 못하다.", "example_in_sentence": "찾지 못하는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 찾지 못하다 → 찾지 못하는 배달 기사들 = delivery workers who can''t find (it).", "example_in_sentence": "찾지 못하는 배달 기사들"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 위해 (for the sake of; for)", "exp": "Indicates purpose or beneficiary. Shows action is done on behalf of someone.", "example_in_sentence": "기사들을 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요 (polite present ending)", "exp": "Verb 날리다 → 날려요.", "example_in_sentence": "날려요"}]}, {"text": "이 남성의 집은 찾기가 어려워요.", "translation": "This man''s house is difficult to find.", "vocab": [{"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find"}, {"ko": "어렵다", "en": "to be difficult"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기가 (nominalizer + subject particle)", "exp": "Converts verb 찾다 into noun form 찾기; ~가 marks it as subject of 어렵다.", "example_in_sentence": "찾기가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (polite ending)", "exp": "The everyday polite ending. 어렵다 is ㅂ irregular: 어렵다 → 어려워요 = is difficult.", "example_in_sentence": "어려워요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 배달 음식이나 택배가 자주 늦게 와요.", "translation": "So delivery food or packages often come late.", "vocab": [{"ko": "배달", "en": "delivery"}, {"ko": "음식", "en": "food"}, {"ko": "택배", "en": "parcel"}, {"ko": "자주", "en": "often"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~이나 (or; either...or)", "exp": "Coordinates two items as alternatives or examples.", "example_in_sentence": "음식이나 택배가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (polite ending)", "exp": "The everyday polite ending. 오다 → 와요 (오 + 아요 becomes 와요) = come.", "example_in_sentence": "와요"}]}, {"text": "배달 기사들이 길을 잃어버리기 때문이에요.", "translation": "It is because delivery workers lose their way.", "vocab": [{"ko": "배달", "en": "delivery"}, {"ko": "길", "en": "way; road"}, {"ko": "잃어버리다", "en": "to lose"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "길을 잃다 (to lose one''s way; to get lost)", "exp": "Idiomatic expression meaning to become lost or unable to find direction.", "example_in_sentence": "길을 잃어버리기"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~기 때문이다 (because; it is because)", "exp": "Nominalizer ~기 + reason marker 때문 + copula 이다, indicating cause/reason.", "example_in_sentence": "잃어버리기 때문이에요"}]}, {"text": "그는 드론에 불빛을 달았어요.", "translation": "He attached a light to the drone.", "vocab": [{"ko": "드론", "en": "drone"}, {"ko": "불빛", "en": "light"}, {"ko": "달다", "en": "to attach; to install"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past polite ending)", "exp": "Indicates completed action in past. Verb 달다 → 달았어요.", "example_in_sentence": "달았어요"}]}, {"text": "배달 기사가 오면 드론을 하늘에 띄워요.", "translation": "When a delivery worker comes, he sends the drone up into the sky.", "vocab": [{"ko": "배달", "en": "delivery"}, {"ko": "드론", "en": "drone"}, {"ko": "하늘", "en": "sky"}, {"ko": "띄우다", "en": "to fly (a drone); to send up"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (when, if)", "exp": "Sets up a condition or time. 오다 → 오면 = when (a worker) comes.", "example_in_sentence": "오면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요 (polite present ending)", "exp": "Verb 띄우다 → 띄워요.", "example_in_sentence": "띄워요"}]}, {"text": "드론이 집까지 길을 안내해 주는 거예요.", "translation": "The drone guides the way all the way to the house.", "vocab": [{"ko": "드론", "en": "drone"}, {"ko": "집", "en": "house"}, {"ko": "길", "en": "way; road"}, {"ko": "안내하다", "en": "to guide"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~까지 (up to; all the way to)", "exp": "Indicates destination or extent, showing direction continues to that point.", "example_in_sentence": "집까지"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~아/어 주다 (to do for someone)", "exp": "Shows that an action helps someone. 안내하다 → 안내해 주다 = to guide (them).", "example_in_sentence": "안내해 주는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 거예요 (explaining)", "exp": "Explains how something works. 안내해 주다 → 안내해 주는 거예요 = (that''s how) it guides (them).", "example_in_sentence": "안내해 주는 거예요"}]}, {"text": "이 방법은 정말 효과적이에요.", "translation": "This method is really effective.", "vocab": [{"ko": "방법", "en": "method"}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really"}, {"ko": "효과적이다", "en": "to be effective"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요 (is)", "exp": "The polite form of 이다 (to be). 효과적 + 이에요 = is effective.", "example_in_sentence": "효과적이에요"}]}, {"text": "이제 배달 기사들이 쉽게 집을 찾을 수 있어요.", "translation": "Now delivery workers can easily find houses.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이제", "en": "now"}, {"ko": "배달", "en": "delivery"}, {"ko": "쉽다", "en": "to be easy"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "Says someone is able to do something. After a consonant use 을: 찾다 → 찾을 수 있어요 = can find.", "example_in_sentence": "찾을 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "배달도 빨리 받을 수 있게 됐어요.", "translation": "He has also become able to get his deliveries quickly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "배달", "en": "delivery"}, {"ko": "빨리", "en": "quickly"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive"}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~도 (also; as well)", "exp": "Additive particle adding subject 배달 to previous context about 집을 찾을 수.", "example_in_sentence": "배달도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있게 되다 (to become able to)", "exp": "Shows gaining an ability. 받다 → 받을 수 있게 됐어요 = became able to receive.", "example_in_sentence": "받을 수 있게 됐어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "캘리포니아", "en": "California", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배달", "en": "delivery", "note": ""}, {"ko": "드론", "en": "drone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어렵다", "en": "to be difficult", "note": ""}, {"ko": "음식", "en": "food", "note": ""}, {"ko": "택배", "en": "parcel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자주", "en": "often", "note": ""}, {"ko": "길", "en": "way; road", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잃어버리다", "en": "to lose", "note": ""}, {"ko": "불빛", "en": "light", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달다", "en": "to attach; to install", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하늘", "en": "sky", "note": ""}, {"ko": "띄우다", "en": "to fly (a drone); to send up", "note": ""}, {"ko": "집", "en": "house", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안내하다", "en": "to guide", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really", "note": ""}, {"ko": "효과적이다", "en": "to be effective", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이제", "en": "now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쉽다", "en": "to be easy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빨리", "en": "quickly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become", "note": ""}, {"word": "길을 잃어버리다", "reading": "gireul ileobeorida", "meaning": "to get lost; to lose one''s way", "context": "배달 기사들이 길을 잃어버리기 때문이에요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~는 (present noun modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes the noun that follows. 찾지 못하다 → 찾지 못하는 배달 기사들 = delivery workers who can''t find (it).", "ex_ko": "미국 캘리포니아에 사는 한 남성이 특별한 방법을 사용해요.", "ex_en": "A man living in California, USA uses a special method."}, {"name": "~어요 (polite present ending)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Indicates statement in polite/conversational tone. Verb 사용하다 → 사용해요.", "ex_ko": "미국 캘리포니아에 사는 한 남성이 특별한 방법을 사용해요.", "ex_en": "A man living in California, USA uses a special method."}, {"name": "~지 못하다 (negation with inability)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Indicates inability or failure to perform an action. Verb 찾다 → 찾지 못하다.", "ex_ko": "집을 찾지 못하는 배달 기사들을 위해 드론(drone)을 날려요.", "ex_en": "He flies a drone for delivery workers who can''t find his house."}, {"name": "~기가 (nominalizer + subject particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Converts verb 찾다 into noun form 찾기; ~가 marks it as subject of 어렵다.", "ex_ko": "이 남성의 집은 찾기가 어려워요.", "ex_en": "This man''s house is difficult to find."}, {"name": "~아/어요 (polite ending)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "The everyday polite ending. 어렵다 is ㅂ irregular: 어렵다 → 어려워요 = is difficult.", "ex_ko": "이 남성의 집은 찾기가 어려워요.", "ex_en": "This man''s house is difficult to find."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past polite ending)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Indicates completed action in past. Verb 달다 → 달았어요.", "ex_ko": "그는 드론에 불빛을 달았어요.", "ex_en": "He attached a light to the drone."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (when, if)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Sets up a condition or time. 오다 → 오면 = when (a worker) comes.", "ex_ko": "배달 기사가 오면 드론을 하늘에 띄워요.", "ex_en": "When a delivery worker comes, he sends the drone up into the sky."}, {"name": "~는 거예요 (explaining)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Explains how something works. 안내해 주다 → 안내해 주는 거예요 = (that''s how) it guides (them).", "ex_ko": "드론이 집까지 길을 안내해 주는 거예요.", "ex_en": "The drone guides the way all the way to the house."}, {"name": "~이에요 (is)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "The polite form of 이다 (to be). 효과적 + 이에요 = is effective.", "ex_ko": "이 방법은 정말 효과적이에요.", "ex_en": "This method is really effective."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Says someone is able to do something. After a consonant use 을: 찾다 → 찾을 수 있어요 = can find.", "ex_ko": "이제 배달 기사들이 쉽게 집을 찾을 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Now delivery workers can easily find houses."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있게 되다 (to become able to)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows gaining an ability. 받다 → 받을 수 있게 됐어요 = became able to receive.", "ex_ko": "배달도 빨리 받을 수 있게 됐어요.", "ex_en": "He has also become able to get his deliveries quickly."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mom3tlzswxz4' and md5(translation) = 'caf77008f086cd4cc66ef9bd15ffdb7f';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There is one gorilla living at Taipei Zoo. This gorilla is female. The gorilla did something special. The gorilla tries to get out of its enclosure. It tries to escape by using a log. It uses the log as a stepping stone. The gorilla is a really smart animal. It can think like a human. It even knows how to use tools. The zookeepers are watching over the gorilla. They help make sure the gorilla doesn''t get hurt. The gorilla''s health and safety are important.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "타이베이 동물원에 고릴라 한 마리가 살아요.", "translation": "A gorilla lives in Taipei Zoo.", "vocab": [{"ko": "타이베이", "en": "Taipei"}, {"ko": "동물원", "en": "zoo"}, {"ko": "고릴라", "en": "gorilla"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "에", "exp": "Location particle marking where an action occurs or where someone/something exists.", "example_in_sentence": "타이베이 동물원에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (polite ending)", "exp": "The everyday polite ending. 살다 has ㅏ, so it takes 아요: 살다 → 살아요 = lives.", "example_in_sentence": "살아요"}]}, {"text": "이 고릴라는 암컷이에요.", "translation": "This gorilla is female.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이", "en": "this"}, {"ko": "암컷", "en": "female"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "는", "exp": "Topic particle marking the subject with contrastive or neutral topic focus.", "example_in_sentence": "이 고릴라는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Copula (descriptive ending for nouns). 암컷 + 이에요 = identifying/defining.", "example_in_sentence": "암컷이에요"}]}, {"text": "고릴라가 특별한 일을 했어요.", "translation": "The gorilla did something special.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing; work"}, {"ko": "하다", "en": "to do"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "가", "exp": "Subject particle marking the agent/doer of the action.", "example_in_sentence": "고릴라가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Describing words take ~(으)ㄴ before a noun. 특별하다 → 특별한 일 = something special.", "example_in_sentence": "특별한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 하다 → 했어요 (completed action).", "example_in_sentence": "했어요"}]}, {"text": "고릴라가 우리에서 나가려고 해요.", "translation": "The gorilla is trying to get out of the enclosure.", "vocab": [{"ko": "우리", "en": "cage; enclosure"}, {"ko": "나가다", "en": "to go out; to exit"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "에서", "exp": "Locational source particle marking where an action starts or originates from.", "example_in_sentence": "우리에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고 하다 (to try to)", "exp": "Shows an attempt or intention. 나가다 → 나가려고 해요 = is trying to get out.", "example_in_sentence": "나가려고 해요"}]}, {"text": "통나무를 이용해서 탈출하려고 해요.", "translation": "It is trying to escape by using a log.", "vocab": [{"ko": "통나무", "en": "log; trunk"}, {"ko": "이용하다", "en": "to use; to utilize"}, {"ko": "탈출하다", "en": "to escape"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "를", "exp": "Direct object particle marking the thing being used.", "example_in_sentence": "통나무를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (by ~ing)", "exp": "Shows how something is done. 이용하다 → 이용해서 = by using.", "example_in_sentence": "이용해서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려고 하다 (to try to)", "exp": "Shows an attempt or intention. 탈출하다 → 탈출하려고 해요 = is trying to escape.", "example_in_sentence": "탈출하려고 해요"}]}, {"text": "통나무를 발판으로 써요.", "translation": "It uses the log as a foothold.", "vocab": [{"ko": "발판", "en": "foothold; stepping stone; base"}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (as)", "exp": "Marks the role something is used for. After a consonant use 으로: 발판 → 발판으로 = as a foothold.", "example_in_sentence": "발판으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (polite ending)", "exp": "The everyday polite ending. 쓰다 → 써요 (the ㅡ drops) = uses.", "example_in_sentence": "써요"}]}, {"text": "고릴라는 정말 똑똑한 동물이에요.", "translation": "The gorilla is truly an intelligent animal.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정말", "en": "really; truly"}, {"ko": "똑똑하다", "en": "to be smart; to be intelligent"}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Describing words take ~(으)ㄴ before a noun. 똑똑하다 → 똑똑한 동물 = a smart animal.", "example_in_sentence": "똑똑한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Copula for nouns. Identifies/defines the subject.", "example_in_sentence": "동물이에요"}]}, {"text": "사람처럼 생각할 수 있어요.", "translation": "It can think like a human.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람", "en": "person; human"}, {"ko": "생각하다", "en": "to think"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "처럼", "exp": "Postposition meaning ''like'' or ''similar to''. Marks comparison.", "example_in_sentence": "사람처럼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "Says someone is able to do something. 생각하다 → 생각할 수 있어요 = can think.", "example_in_sentence": "생각할 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "도구를 사용할 줄도 알아요.", "translation": "It also knows how to use tools.", "vocab": [{"ko": "도구", "en": "tool"}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use"}, {"ko": "알다", "en": "to know"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 줄 알다 (to know how to)", "exp": "Says someone knows how to do something. 사용하다 → 사용할 줄 알아요 = knows how to use.", "example_in_sentence": "사용할 줄도 알아요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "도", "exp": "Additive particle meaning ''also; too.'' Shows addition to prior statement.", "example_in_sentence": "줄도"}]}, {"text": "동물원 사람들이 고릴라를 지켜보고 있어요.", "translation": "Zoo staff are keeping an eye on the gorilla.", "vocab": [{"ko": "동물원", "en": "zoo"}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person; people"}, {"ko": "지켜보다", "en": "to watch over; to observe carefully"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "이/가 (subject particle)", "exp": "Marks the subject. After a consonant use 이: 사람들 → 사람들이.", "example_in_sentence": "사람들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "를", "exp": "Direct object particle marking the thing being watched.", "example_in_sentence": "고릴라를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Shows ongoing/continuous action. 지켜보다 → 지켜보고 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "지켜보고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "고릴라가 다치지 않게 도와줘요.", "translation": "They help so that the gorilla does not get hurt.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다치다", "en": "to be injured; to get hurt"}, {"ko": "도와주다", "en": "to help; to assist"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않게 (so that ~ not)", "exp": "Describes the purpose of an action: so that something does not happen. 다치다 → 다치지 않게 = so that (it) doesn''t get hurt.", "example_in_sentence": "다치지 않게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (polite ending)", "exp": "The everyday polite ending. 도와주다 → 도와줘요 (주 + 어요 becomes 줘요) = help.", "example_in_sentence": "도와줘요"}]}, {"text": "고릴라의 건강과 안전이 중요해요.", "translation": "The gorilla''s health and safety are important.", "vocab": [{"ko": "건강", "en": "health"}, {"ko": "안전", "en": "safety"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "의", "exp": "Possessive/genitive particle marking possession or relationship.", "example_in_sentence": "고릴라의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "과", "exp": "Coordinating conjunction meaning ''and.'' Joins two nouns.", "example_in_sentence": "건강과 안전이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요 (polite ending)", "exp": "The everyday polite ending. 하다 words become 해요: 중요하다 → 중요해요 = is important.", "example_in_sentence": "중요해요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "타이베이", "en": "Taipei", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물원", "en": "zoo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고릴라", "en": "gorilla", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이", "en": "this", "note": ""}, {"ko": "암컷", "en": "female", "not