l to Busan.", "ex_ko": "서울에서 부산까지 2시간 반이면 갈 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "You can go from Seoul to Busan in two and a half hours."}, {"name": "~(이)면", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''if it is''. With an amount of time it means ''in just that much time''. 2시간 반이면 = in two and a half hours.", "ex_ko": "서울에서 부산까지 2시간 반이면 갈 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "You can go from Seoul to Busan in two and a half hours."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Auxiliary expressing possibility or ability. 가다 (to go) + ㄹ 수 있어요 = can go.", "ex_ko": "서울에서 부산까지 2시간 반이면 갈 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "You can go from Seoul to Busan in two and a half hours."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Coordinating connective joining two actions in sequence. 보다 (to watch) + 고 + 놀라워했어요 (were surprised) = watched and were surprised.", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이 영상을 보고 놀라워했어요.", "ex_en": "Many people watched this video and were surprised."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense ending. 놀라워하다 (to be surprised) + 았어요 = were surprised (in past).", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이 영상을 보고 놀라워했어요.", "ex_en": "Many people watched this video and were surprised."}, {"name": "~라는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Quotative modifier meaning ''that says/means''. Quote + 라는 = that says (modifying 댓글/comment).", "ex_ko": "\"정말 빠르다\", \"신기하다\"라는 댓글이 많았어요.", "ex_en": "There were many comments saying \"Really fast\" and \"Amazing.\""}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Possibility modifier. 실감하다 (to actually feel) + ㄹ 수 있는 = that allows (you) to actually feel.", "ex_ko": "고속열차의 빠른 속도를 실감할 수 있는 영상이에요.", "ex_en": "It is a video that allows you to actually feel the fast speed of the high-speed train."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mon2hyujdczj' and md5(translation) = 'a9a80f2b204d5895e2896aa7ada27850';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "오래된 사진 한 장이 인터넷에서 인기예요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "An old photograph is popular on the internet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old", "note": "describes something that has existed for a long time"}, {"ko": "인기", "en": "popularity", "note": "noun meaning ''being well-liked or popular''"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 것 (nominalizer / modifier)", "exp": "A past participle modifies the following noun.", "example_in_sentence": "오래된 사진"}, {"pattern": "~예요 (polite copula)", "exp": "Polite present statement, equivalent to ~입니다 in formal speech.", "example_in_sentence": "인기예요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "1895년에 찍은 인도 파트나라는 도시 사진이에요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "It is a photograph of a city called Patna, India, taken in 1895.", "vocab": [{"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (a photo)", "note": "verb for capturing images with a camera"}, {"ko": "인도", "en": "India", "note": "proper noun: the country"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 것 (nominalizer / modifier)", "exp": "Past participle modifying the noun that follows.", "example_in_sentence": "1895년에 찍은 인도 파트나라는 도시 사진"}, {"pattern": "~이에요 (polite copula)", "exp": "Polite present statement used after a noun ending in a consonant.", "example_in_sentence": "사진이에요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "파트나는 인도에 있는 큰 도시예요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "Patna is a large city in India.", "vocab": [{"ko": "크다", "en": "to be big; large", "note": "adjective describing size"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 것 (nominalizer / modifier)", "exp": "Past participle used as a modifier.", "example_in_sentence": "인도에 있는 큰 도시"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "130년 전 모습이 사진에 담겨 있어요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "The photo captures what the city looked like 130 years ago.", "vocab": [{"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance; look", "note": "noun meaning how something looks"}, {"ko": "담기다", "en": "to be contained; to be captured", "note": "passive verb meaning something is held or recorded in something"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~아/어 있다 (resultative)", "exp": "Describes a state resulting from a completed action.", "example_in_sentence": "담겨 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "그때는 카메라가 아주 귀했어요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "Back then, cameras were very rare.", "vocab": [{"ko": "귀하다", "en": "to be rare; precious", "note": "adjective meaning scarce or valuable"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~았/었어요 (past polite)", "exp": "Past polite statement; indicates a past state or action.", "example_in_sentence": "귀했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "사진을 본 사람들이 놀라고 있어요.", "idx": 5, "translation": "People who saw the photograph are amazed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놀라다", "en": "to be surprised; amazed", "note": "verb describing a state of astonishment"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 것 (nominalizer / modifier)", "exp": "Past participle modifying the noun.", "example_in_sentence": "사진을 본 사람들"}, {"pattern": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "exp": "Progressive or continuous action; an ongoing state.", "example_in_sentence": "놀라고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "\"옛날 모습이 신기하다\"고 말해요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "They say, ''The old appearance is fascinating.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be interesting; fascinating", "note": "adjective meaning remarkable or surprising in a good way"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다고 하다 (reported speech)", "exp": "Reports what someone said or claims.", "example_in_sentence": "\"옛날 모습이 신기하다\"고 말해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "건물과 사람들의 옷차림이 지금과 달라요.", "idx": 7, "translation": "The buildings and people''s clothing are different from now.", "vocab": [{"ko": "건물", "en": "building", "note": "noun for structures"}, {"ko": "옷차림", "en": "clothing; outfit; dress", "note": "noun meaning how someone is dressed"}, {"ko": "다르다", "en": "to be different", "note": "adjective meaning not the same"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~와/과 (conjunction: and; with)", "exp": "Connects two nouns or subjects.", "example_in_sentence": "건물과 사람들의 옷차림"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "오래된 사진은 역사를 배울 수 있게 